    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.misc\n\n### Description\n\n`setup_restore_cursor()` neither unfolds folds nor centers screen on line after opening the file with folds\r\n\r\n`minimal.lua`:\r\n```\r\n-- Bootstrap lazy.nvim\r\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath \"data\" .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n    vim.fn.system {\r\n        \"git\",\r\n        \"clone\",\r\n        \"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n        \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\r\n        \"--branch=stable\", -- latest stable release\r\n        lazypath,\r\n    }\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\r\n    {\r\n        \"echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\r\n        version = false,\r\n        config = function()\r\n            require(\"mini.misc\").setup()\r\n            MiniMisc.setup_restore_cursor()\r\n        end,\r\n    },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.0-dev-565+g3688735c2b\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Open any file with latest position being inside folds\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nFolds don't get unfolded, window is not centered at last line",
